    "body": "Not sure `script`'s `baseURL` is valid here -- we just created `script` in the first step of this algorithm and haven't initialized that field yet.\r\n\r\nI see that other \"create a module script\" algos take the baseURL as a parameter, e.g. see [create a javascript module script](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#creating-a-javascript-module-script). It looks to me like \"create a CSS module script\" also needs that parameter. We'd pass in the \"response's URL\" as the baseURL [here](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#fetching-scripts:creating-a-css-module-script) in the same way as is done for WASM module scripts and JS module scripts nearby.\r\n\r\nIt's a little more plumbing than I thought it'd be in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11629#issuecomment-3276624308 but I hadn't realized at the time that the CSS module script's baseURL just gets set to null.",
    "created_at": "2025-09-25T21:22:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-25T21:22:54Z",
